/* List with selection:
   <div class="nui-list">
       <div class="nui-list__viewport">
           <div class="nui-list__item nui-anim" data-for="row : rows"
                data-class-is-selected="row.id == selected"
                data-event-click="select(row.id)">{{ row.name }}</div>
       </div>
   </div>
   The rounded frame (.nui-list) does not clip; the square viewport inside
   it scrolls. An element that clips with a border-radius needs the stencil
   clip mask on every frame, a square one only the scissor. The frame's
   padding (4dp) is more than its inner radius (3dp), so rows never reach the
   rounded corners. Give the viewport a height (or max-height) in the
   window's sheet to scroll: .my-list .nui-list__viewport { height: ...; }.
   The `disabled` attribute takes a row out of hit testing, the tab order and
   Enter/Space, like a disabled button. Enter and Space select the row that
   has the keyboard focus (see docs/ui/AUTHORING.md "Keyboard and modals").
   is-hover and is-focus force a state without the pointer or the keyboard. */

.nui-list
{
	display: block;
	padding: 0;
	background-color: transparent;
	border-width: 0;
	border-color: var(--border);
	border-radius: 0;
}

.nui-list__viewport
{
	display: block;
	overflow-y: auto;
}

.nui-list__item
{
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: row;
	align-items: center;
	gap: var(--space-2);
	box-sizing: border-box;
	min-height: 24dp;
	padding: 0 8dp;
	/* The left edge is the selection stripe; the focus ring uses all four, so
	   they are reserved here and focus does not move the row. RmlUi paints the
	   background inside the border, so a transparent edge shows the list. */
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: transparent;
	border-radius: 6dp;
	color: var(--text);
	tab-index: auto;
}
.nui-list__item:hover, .nui-list__item.is-hover
{
	background-color: var(--surface-hover);
}
.nui-list__item.is-selected
{
	background-color: var(--selection);
	border-color: transparent;
	color: var(--accent);
	font-weight: bold;
}
/* After is-selected: both weigh the same, so the later rule wins. */
.nui-list__item:focus-visible, .nui-list__item.is-focus
{
	border-color: var(--focus-ring);
}
/* A focused selected row keeps its stripe (the heavier selector). */
.nui-list__item.is-selected:focus-visible, .nui-list__item.is-selected.is-focus
{
	border-left-color: var(--accent);
}
.nui-list__item[disabled]
{
	color: var(--text-muted);
	pointer-events: none;
	tab-index: none;
	focus: none;
}
/* Hover fade (--dur-fast, --ease-out). */
.nui-list__item.nui-anim
{
	transition: background-color border-color 0.1s cubic-out;
}

.nui-list__label
{
	flex: 1 1 auto;
}
.nui-list__meta
{
	color: var(--text-muted);
	font-size: var(--font-sm);
}
